                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Really glad I got to play all these classics. The UI is not the best but it works I guess. Has gallery, music and history of the franchise to check out, interesting stuff. Didn't try online.\r\n\r\nIn this collection I didn't play the first Street Fighter because I've already played it from that arcade stadium game from capcom. I also played SF 2 but in this collection I tried SF 2 ST.\r\n\r\nSpeaking of Super Turbo, what the hell was that CPU difficulty? First I thought that I was pretty bad but I was really trying, doing some nice moves and stuff. Turns out, this port actually is messed up and the bots are crazy hard. I couldn't pass the second stage...\r\n\r\nAnyway, then I went for the Alphas. Visuals improved, more anime-like. Music is awesome! I really loved the OST from 1 and 2. There were those alpha counters aswell. Each time I landed one I got overjoyed. Hard bosses, had to deal with Bison a couple of times. Nice mechanic of powering your supers and special moves. I think SF6 has this kinda implemented.\r\n\r\nAnd for the Street Fighter 3 trilogy, damn that animation boost. Bunch of frames were made so the characters were moving pretty smooth. Lots of new characters. Music is really good, especially Third Strike. Like a mix of hip-hop with jazz and funk, crazy good. The other two were ok. The gameplay of all 3 were kinda similar because of the Super Arts and parries, but in Third Strike you can even parry stunned. Parrying is so fun to do, it's hard tho. Also, FUCK THAT GILL BOSS. Pain in the ass. Had to deal with him 3 times, because it's the same boss for all three...",
